From 10727209f8a197d107e0a902fca2efaaf3553b1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:34:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 081/101] script: IScene.createModelData, IModelData and model
 layers from script geometry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

createModelData (d.ts 2.8) builds a model from a script's buffers: per shape a Float32Array
vertexBuffer laid out as its vertexFormat (IModelData.POSITION 3, NORMAL 3, TANGENT_SIGNED 4,
UV 2, COLOR 4 floats, in that order), an optional Uint32Array / Uint16Array indexBuffer (none:
the vertices in threes) and a material (a path or an IAssetHandle). The scene holds it;
createLayer (data) or createLayer ({ model: data, … }) makes a model layer of it
(`__modeldata/<id>`), drawn as a model's meshes are. IModelData.applyData changes only what a
shape names and re-uploads that layer's buffers (dynamic buffers); replaceData rebuilds the
layer's meshes (shapes may be added, a null one removed). destroyModelData drops the data; a
layer keeps the copy it built. IModelData.POSITION … COLOR are on the class and its instances.

A model layer is a ScriptableObject now (getLayer and createLayer return it). In a 2D scene a
model draws in WE's world pixels (y up; "1 unit = 1 pixel") through the layers' projection.
Ours: its z is squashed into that projection's depth range and the 2D target has no depth
buffer, so faces draw in index order; the boundingBox members are ignored. COLOR is read past
(Puppet's vertex has no colour). Scene natives are configurable now (builtins.js wraps
createLayer).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F4 (createModelData)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
